# Intent: Turning toward a person, on the unit (owner brief 2026-11-17). A task of priority 1 on core 0 (below the face loop and the servo task at 3 on core 1, and the audio tasks) with a 6 KB stack in PSRAM (the 4 KB first tried left a margin of 964 bytes on the unit, under the 1,024 floor; the log line's float formatting is the deep part) and its state (about 8 KB) in PSRAM: internal RAM costs only the task control block, under 1 KB, so the steady use is far below the 3 KB budget. It runs the wire core (S13) every 50 ms while a look is going on and every 250 ms at rest, wakes at once on the wake word (maipai_listen_wake calls maipai_seek_addressed, a touch that starts a listen counts too), reads the saved setting turn_to_faces (off, talk, default talk, always) through the cached reader maipai_tb_prefs (a PSRAM stack never reads flash: patches FM05 and TC02; the lint scripts/psram-stack-lint.py walks this task), reads the gates (awake and not the sleeping face, mute, vision off, full quiet, screen off as privacy sleep, quiet hours as the slower speed), runs the camera burst of the core (camera-on cue first, one 40 by 30 gray picture, dropped), and moves the head through the same gate a person's head move has (the remote-session gate of patch FM03, source user so the idle-look rule never drops it, speed 150 times the core's percent, minimum 100, pan only). The head's settled state is read from the animation value (the servo's moving flag reads the bus and is not polled). Tools: self.look.claim (owner, ttl_s 5 to 60, 0 is 15), self.look.release, self.look.status (owner unit, host or none, enabled, setting, state, last face and last mover ago, counters, fov_deg, x_sign, calibration state) and self.look.calibrate (the owner's later run: pans through known angles and watches the scene shift, prints and returns the numbers, applies them to the running seeker unless apply is false; it asks nothing of a person except a still room with something in view). The face detector is not part of the image: Kconfig MAIPAI_FACE_DETECT (default n) is reserved and stops the build with the reason when set, because the model has no flash room without giving up pack cache (docs/design/face-seek-2026-11-17.md section 11).
# Placement: unit (the seeker runs on the robot and is complete with no host; a host only holds the lease)
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/maipai_listen.cc, maipai_tbprefs.{h,cc}, hal_mcp.cpp, Kconfig.projbuild (ours, patches TB01, TB04, S11); new files hal/maipai_seek.{h,cc}
# Check after a flash: self.look.status answers owner unit and setting talk; self.look.claim from the host gives owner host and the unit seeks no more; a wake word with a person moving in view turns the head toward them and the camera cue shows for every burst; mute, vision off, full quiet and the screen off stop every camera read and head move; internal free and the largest internal block do not fall (the memory line before and after a spoken turn); the log shows one MAIPAI-SEEK line per decision; self.look.calibrate in a still lit room ends with result ok, sign and fov_deg.

